  "released": "2026-08-26",
  "changelog": "v229: the ear speaks claims \u2014 every fact, one record, one receipt (wave C, item C3 of the audited final timeline build plan, \u00a72.1, \u00a76.1, \u00a76.4 and owner amendment 2). WHY: v220 froze what a temporal interpretation IS and v221 put one on disk, and nothing yet SAID one \u2014 the two passes that actually listen to people, the focused landmark recorder and the general listener, could only emit a LADDER ROW. A ladder row belongs to a domain and carries at most one date, so \u2018we moved when James was two\u2019 had no shape (no date) and \u2018my neighbour's boy was born in 2019\u2019 had no home (no domain), and the listener leaf said in so many words to leave the first one out: leave the record undated and the arithmetic will reach it later. The arithmetic never reached it, because nothing gave it anything to reach. The plan calls both of those usable information (\u00a72.1: capture is NOT restricted to family; \u00a76.4: relative phrasings must be RETAINED even when they cannot yet be placed), and dropping them is the defect the whole substrate exists to end. So BOTH LEAVES GAINED A `claims` LIST in `temporal_claims`' own vocabulary \u2014 claim type, subject mention in the person's own words, event kind, temporal value, and a bounded quotation without which the claim is refused. BRIDGING, NOT BIG-BANG: the list is emitted BESIDE the landmark records and never instead of them, `timeline.save_landmark` keeps its signature and its meaning, and every stored pre-v229 completion parses byte-for-byte as it did \u2014 a completion with no `claims` key yields an empty `RecorderOutcome.claims`, which is the LAST field of that dataclass for exactly that reason. THE DRAFT AND THE BINDING. `validate_temporal_claim` requires four things the EAR cannot know \u2014 the vault `source_ref` (the message is not a source until it is promoted), the extractor version, the creation time, and the claim id derived from the first two \u2014 so a claim is parsed as a DRAFT through that same one door against a NAMED unbound placeholder, stripped of exactly those four fields, and BOUND when the source exists. There is no second validator and no second vocabulary; a test pins that binding adds the binding and changes nothing else, and another pins that no placeholder survives it. TWO ROADS INTO ONE SUBSTRATE. v225 flipped the ENTRY store: a landmark record filed through `timeline.save_landmark` is promoted to `sources/landmarks/` and converted by a deterministic RULE. This item adds the other road \u2014 the MESSAGE, promoted to `sources/conversations/` and read by a MODEL \u2014 and a fact stated in a focused landmark turn can therefore reach the active index twice. That is corroboration, not duplication, and the two cannot collide: different source, different revision, different extractor version, therefore different `derive_claim_id`. They are two interpretations of two different sources (\u00a74.1), which is the shape the fold is built for now that v225 moved `chronology.reconcile` to draw time over the live active set. What the model's road carries that the rule's cannot is the reason this item exists: an event kind, an order against another moment, a non-family subject, and the bounded quotation that proves any of it. ONE MESSAGE, ONE SOURCE, ONE RECEIPT, N CLAIMS. `landmark_recorder.file_claims` is the whole write path and it is three lines of binding over `temporal_store.file_message_extraction`: the message is promoted to `sources/conversations/` BEFORE anything cites it (owner amendment 2), every claim from it cites the same revision, the receipt is immutable and idempotent on `derive_extraction_idempotency_key`, and a message that produced no claims files NOTHING \u2014 which is the amendment's own rule and not an optimization. EDITING A LEAF IS A NEW EXTRACTOR: the extractor's prompt version is a digest of the leaf's own bytes, so a prompt edit lands on a new receipt path beside the old one rather than rewriting yesterday's reading \u2014 \u00a71.3's rule, read one step further than the model. THE BACKSTOPS EXTEND RATHER THAN FORK. v218's `listener_heard_nothing` now counts a claim as a thing heard, so a completion speaking ONLY the substrate's vocabulary clears it exactly as a landmark record does and a completion emitting NEITHER shape lints exactly as before \u2014 the question that class asks is *did anything come back*, never *did the old shape come back*. v214's plurality class is read over the claims list as `general_listener.claims_missing_subjects`, a BINDING of that class's two decidable primitives (`_name_groups`, `_record_terms`, both read by name, because a second table of what a name looks like is the recurring defect the doctrine forbids) and never a second copy; it is retryable, never withholding, and it shares the ONE regeneration \u2014 MAX_ATTEMPTS is still 2. THE FOCUSED GUARANTEE IS NOT WEAKENED. `answer_must_record` still reads the RECORDS and only the records: the focused recorder is the canonical writer for a focused turn (\u00a72.1, \u00a76.1), so a claim heard alongside upgrades a terminal from `nothing` to `recorded` and rides out on the outcome, but it never excuses the domain's own missing record. Its LANDMARK list is still locked to the asked domain \u2014 the 2026-08-25 audit's refusal is untouched \u2014 while its CLAIMS list hears the whole message, which is \u00a76.1's own reading: one canonical recorder and one semantic write set for that turn, and the listener must not compete for it. Nine goldens in `claims-extraction-01.json` carry the founder shapes: twelve jobs become twelve `job` claims, four children become four `identity` claims AND four `child_born` dated claims (never an aggregate \u2014 the contract's own `aggregate_subject_mention` refusal makes that a mechanism rather than a paragraph), the relative move is retained undated, the neighbour's child is refused as a roster row and kept as a claim, and silence still withholds. ONE PRESCREEN AMENDMENT, measured on this branch and fixed rather than filed: every age table in `may_contain_datable` \u2014 borrowed and local alike \u2014 anchored on a LEADING conjunction (\"when I was twelve\"), because that is the order a moment FRAGMENT is written in, and a MESSAGE is written in either order. *\"I was about twelve when we left the farm\"* fired nothing at all, which under-fires in the direction the module itself calls expensive. Two patterns join `THIRD_PERSON_AGE_RES`: subject + was/were + age + `when`, and subject + was/were + an APPROXIMATOR + age. The `when` and the approximator are what keep a number an age and not a count \u2014 \"there were three of us\", \"it was about 12 dollars\" and \"the box was almost 3 feet wide\" are pinned NEGATIVE beside the new positives, and all 34 pre-existing prescreen cases are unchanged. THE HONEST COST: both leaves roughly doubled, ~1150 to ~2000 tokens, and the size pins say so in full. They still carry no identity, no behavior, no examples and no transcript, which is the only property those pins have ever held \u2014 a ceiling that forced the contract to be incomplete would be buying tokens with dropped facts. Identity resolution, the calculated timeline and the work-item surfaces remain waves C-remainder, D and F.",
